{"id":96,"flavor":[{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!"],"text":"If you sleep by it all the time, it will sometimes show you dreams it had eaten in the past."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"It puts its prey to sleep and devours their dreams. It seems that bad dreams taste sour, so Drowzee doesn’t particularly like eating them."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"It can be spotted near recreational facilities, intending to eat the pleasant dreams of children who enjoyed themselves there that day."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"It finds really fun dreams tasty. When it makes friends with people, it may show them the most delicious dreams it’s ever eaten."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"A Pokémon that nourishes itself by eating dreams, it is thought to share common ancestry with Munna and Musharna."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Omega Ruby","Sapphire","Ruby"],"text":"If your nose becomes itchy while you are sleeping, it’s a sure sign that one of these Pokémon is standing above your pillow and trying to eat your dream through your nostrils."},{"games":["Y","HeartGold","Gold"],"text":"If you think that you had a good dream but you can’t remember it, a Drowzee has probably eaten it."},{"games":["X","LeafGreen"],"text":"Puts enemies to sleep, then eats their dreams. Occasionally gets sick from eating only bad dreams."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"It can tell what people are dreaming by sniffing with its big nose. It loves fun dreams."},{"games":["SoulSilver","Silver"],"text":"It remembers every dream it eats. It rarely eats the dreams of adults because children’s are much tastier."},{"games":["FireRed"],"text":"A descendent of the legendary animal baku, which is said to eat dreams. It is skilled at hypnotism."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"If your nose becomes itchy while you are sleeping, it’s a sure sign that a DROWZEE is standing above your pillow and trying to eat your dream through your nostrils."},{"games":["Crystal"],"text":"When it twitches its nose, it can tell where someone is sleeping and what that person is dreaming about."},{"games":["Yellow"],"text":"If you sleep by it all the time, it will sometimes show you dreams it has eaten in the past."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Insomnia","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon's insomnia prevents it from falling asleep."},{"name":"Forewarn","hidden":false,"description":"When it enters a battle, the Pokémon can tell one of the moves an opposing Pokémon has."},{"name":"Inner Focus","hidden":true,"description":"The Pokémon's intense focus prevents it from flinching or being affected by Intimidate."}],"eggGroups":["Human-Like"],"genderRate":4,"hatchCounter":20,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"medium","habitat":"grassland","color":"Yellow","shape":"Humanoid","evolution":{"id":96,"name":"Drowzee","condition":null,"children":[{"id":97,"name":"Hypno","condition":"Lv. 26","children":[]}]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[1,1],[1,95],[5,50],[9,93],[13,29],[17,139],[21,60],[25,244],[29,428],[33,207],[37,94],[41,417],[45,473],[49,248]],"machine":[34,280,347,174,605,38,409,577,227,283,203,797,263,7,374,411,264,492,248,447,114,270,8,286,282,113,67,490,118,417,101,182,60,244,94,917,678,473,240,115,156,247,285,214,500,164,241,129,36,269,851,168,9,86,92,885,271,433,428],"egg":[7,260,385,8,471,427,272,9],"tutor":[]},"cards":[{"id":"sv1-210","name":"Drowzee","set":"Scarlet & Violet","date":"2023-03-31","rarity":"Illustration Rare","number":"210","artist":"Tomokazu Komiya","img":"sv1/210"},{"id":"sv10-79","name":"Team Rocket's Drowzee","set":"Destined Rivals","date":"2025-05-30","rarity":"Common","number":"79","artist":null,"img":"sv10/79"},{"id":"sv6pt5-16","name":"Drowzee","set":"Shrouded Fable","date":"2024-08-02","rarity":"Common","number":"16","artist":"OKUBO","img":"sv6pt5/16"},{"id":"sv3pt5-96","name":"Drowzee","set":"151","date":"2023-09-22","rarity":"Common","number":"96","artist":"Mousho","img":"sv3pt5/96"},{"id":"sv1-8